<title>MEXICO: FORECAST - AVERAGE SURVEY OF MEXICAN INDICATORS.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - AVERAGE SURVEY OF MEXICAN INDICATORS.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are consensus forecasts from a Reuters survey of Mexican economic indicators conducted with the Mexico City offices of 13 brokerages and research firms.</p>
<p>Date   Indicator    Period  Avg Fcast   Median	Previous</p>
<p>14/08  Ind Act	June     8.30 pct   8.20 pct     9.00 pct</p>
<p>20/08  Unemployment July     3.58 pct   3.60 pct     3.40 pct</p>
<p>21/08  Retail Sls   June     4.92 pct   4.80 pct     4.40 pct</p>
<p>21/08  Wholesle Sls June     4.60 pct   4.00 pct    -0.12 pct</p>
<p>21/08* Trade Blc    July  +$107.25 million $100.0 million  +$308 million**</p>
<p>	 Exports	July    $9.147 bln $9.139 bln $9.412 bln**</p>
<p>	 Imports	July    $9.028 bln $9.049 bln $9.113 bln**</p>
<p>19/08  GDP	    Q2	 5.92 pct   5.96 pct	5.1 pct</p>
<p>25/08* Inflation    Aug1-15  0.48 pct   0.48 pct     0.38 pct</p>
<p>----------------------Mexican financial indicators-----------</p>
<p>29/08  28-day Cetes  End Aug  18.67 pct  18.10 pct   17.70</p>
<p>29/08  48-hour peso  End Aug  7.9387	7.9300     7.8175</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    *estimated date    **preliminary figures</p>
<p>((--Caroline Brothers, Mexico City newsroom 525 728-7905))</p>
